## 4️⃣ Booking Tips & Practicalities

| Tip | Details |
|-----|---------|
| **Online tickets** | All museums above (except the Vatican, which requires pre‑booking) sell timed‑entry tickets on their official sites or via Klook. Book at least **48 h** in advance for the Vatican and Borghese. |
| **Roma Pass** | The 48‑hour Roma Pass gives free entry to **Capitoline, Borghese, National Roman Museum (Palazzo Massimo), and MAXXI** (plus unlimited public transport). It does **not** cover the Vatican. |
| **Free cancellation** | Look for the “free_cancellation” label in the API – many tickets (e.g., the Vatican “Vatican City Tickets – Museums & Sistine Chapel”) have it, giving you flexibility if plans change. |
| **Dress code** | The Vatican enforces modest attire (no bare shoulders/shorts). Other museums are casual but comfortable shoes are a must. |
| **Audio guides** | All listed museums provide free audio guides (often included in the ticket price). For the Vatican, the guide is available in 12 languages and can be downloaded to your phone. |
| **Night‑open events** | Borghese, MAXXI and Castel Sant’Angelo occasionally host after‑dark tours – check their calendars if you’re staying late. |

